# At the Crossroads of the Humanities and Healing: Dancing at Two Weddings.

**Authors:** Chavis, Geri Giebel

## Abstract
Argues that the healer acts as the muse of the humanities, while the humanities function as healer's creative force. Describes how the author reached the crossroads of the humanities and healing (as an English professor and a psychotherapist), and examines the work of John Keats. Shows how poetry therapists stand at the crossroads where emotion and language intersect. (SR)

